-- Migration 0012 — explicit privileges for the API roles.
-- Earlier migrations relied on Supabase's default privileges (every new public table granted to
-- anon, authenticated and service_role, then narrowed with revokes). Newer hosted projects do not
-- add those defaults, so the production database had RLS policies but no table privileges at all.
-- This states the final privileges explicitly, generated from the tested local database, so every
-- environment ends up identical. RLS still decides which rows each role can reach.
-- Generated from a fully migrated local stack; re-running is harmless (grants are idempotent).

